LIBPKGAPPLY_EXEC_RESULT_CODEC(3)

# NAME

encode_lifecycle_execution_result, decode_lifecycle_execution_result - retain and reopen exact lifecycle execution evidence

# SYNOPSIS

*#include <libpkgapply-exec/result_codec.h>*

*lifecycle_execution_result_encoding encode_lifecycle_execution_result(const lifecycle_execution_result& result);*

*lifecycle_execution_result decode_lifecycle_execution_result(const lifecycle_execution_result_encoding& encoding, admitted_lifecycle_session session, pkgexec::backend_capability_profile backend);*

# DESCRIPTION

*encode_lifecycle_execution_result*() emits the canonical versioned record for
one retained *lifecycle_execution_result*. The record embeds the canonical
*libpkgexec* execution-result encoding and binds it to the exact lifecycle-node
and adapter-result identities.

*decode_lifecycle_execution_result*() requires the complete admitted lifecycle
session and exact backend capability profile. It verifies the whole-record
checksum, derives the execution request purely from the session, delegates the
embedded execution evidence to *libpkgexec*, reconstructs the adapter result,
checks every retained identity, and requires canonical byte-for-byte
re-encoding.

The codec never serializes or reconstructs application requests, lifecycle
nodes, admitted sessions, execution requests, backend profiles, host paths,
credentials, resource materializations, or backend semantics. Identity strings
are not semantic authority. Decoding does not call *prepare*(3), inspect or
create directories, change ownership, build execution resources, invoke a
backend, execute a program, publish state, or perform any other mutation.

# ERRORS

Malformed, truncated, noncanonical, or internally inconsistent bytes raise
*pkgapply_exec::error* with *corrupt_encoding*. A valid record presented with a
different lifecycle node, execution-session authority, or backend profile
raises *authority_mismatch*. Encoding a result that violates the adapter
contract raises *inconsistent_result*.

# SEE ALSO

*libpkgapply-exec*(7), *pkgexec_result_codec*(3), *libpkgapply*(3), *libpkgexec*(3)
